sequenceDiagram
  autonumber

  actor Filer as Filing Member
  actor Voter as Voting Member
  actor AdminUser as Group Admin
  participant Browser
  participant NextJS as Next.js API
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant Pinata as Pinata IPFS
  participant Queue as BullMQ / Redis
  participant Email as SMTP Server
  participant Sched as Scheduler (Cron)

  Note over Filer,Sched: Dispute Filing

  Filer->>Browser: Navigate to /disputes → "File Dispute"
  Browser-->>Filer: Dispute form
  Filer->>Browser: Fill form + attach evidence file
  Browser->>NextJS: POST /api/disputes

  opt Evidence file attached
    NextJS->>Pinata: Upload file
    Pinata-->>NextJS: { IpfsHash }
    NextJS->>DB: Store evidenceCid
  end

  NextJS->>DB: Create Dispute (OPEN, votingDeadline = now + 72h)
  NextJS->>Queue: Enqueue notifications for all members
  Queue->>NextJS: Process notification job
  NextJS->>DB: Create in-app Notifications
  NextJS->>Email: sendDisputeEmail() to each member
  Email-->>Voter: "New dispute — vote now"
  NextJS-->>Browser: 201 Created { disputeId }

  Note over Filer,Sched: Peer Voting (72-hour window)

  Voter->>Browser: Navigate to /disputes
  Browser->>NextJS: GET /api/disputes
  NextJS->>DB: Fetch open disputes
  DB-->>NextJS: Dispute list
  NextJS-->>Browser: Dispute list

  Voter->>Browser: Cast vote (UPHELD / REJECTED)
  Browser->>NextJS: POST /api/disputes/{id}/vote
  NextJS->>DB: Already voted?

  alt Already voted
    NextJS-->>Browser: 409 Conflict
  else First vote
    NextJS->>DB: Create DisputeVote
    NextJS-->>Browser: 200 OK
  end

  Note over Filer,Sched: Auto-Resolution at Deadline

  Sched->>NextJS: POST /api/cron/reminders (hourly)
  NextJS->>DB: Disputes where deadline <= now AND status = OPEN
  NextJS->>DB: Count UPHELD vs REJECTED votes

  alt UPHELD majority
    NextJS->>DB: Dispute → RESOLVED: UPHELD
  else REJECTED or no quorum
    NextJS->>DB: Dispute → RESOLVED: REJECTED
  end

  NextJS->>Queue: Notify all parties
  Queue-->>Filer: "Dispute resolved"

  Note over Filer,Sched: Admin Force-Resolve

  AdminUser->>Browser: /admin/disputes → "Force Resolve"
  Browser->>NextJS: POST /api/admin/disputes/{id}/resolve
  NextJS->>DB: Dispute → RESOLVED (admin override)
  NextJS->>Queue: Notify all parties
  NextJS-->>Browser: 200 OK
